{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2:_FASTEST_SOLUTION!!!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2: FASTEST SOLUTION!!!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Construction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Construction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular piece of paper whose length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99f089046b752269e77100c333b11d8d72e5895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> times the width has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The paper is divided into three equal sections along the opposite lengths, and then a dotted line is drawn from the first divider to the second divider on the opposite side as shown. The paper is then folded flat along this dotted line to create a new shape with area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. What is the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340318477c3b9b0805b9fd903c3598e4e9ae43ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{B}{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"17\" height=\"37\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/383b46c75e8be868196ec01badfad01411d16223.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; size(6cm);  real L = 0.05;  pair A = (0,0); pair B = (sqrt(3),0); pair C = (sqrt(3),1); pair D = (0,1);  pair X1 = (sqrt(3)/3,0); pair X2= (2*sqrt(3)/3,0); pair Y1 = (2*sqrt(3)/3,1); pair Y2 = (sqrt(3)/3,1);  dot(X1); dot(Y1);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(2)); draw(X1--Y1,dashed);  draw(X2--(2*sqrt(3)/3,L)); draw(Y2--(sqrt(3)/3,1-L)); [/asy]\" width=\"285\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/35101a628139bf11bc3563c2878f5c294f43ea1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the midpoint of the dotted line.  Draw a line perpendicular to it.  From the point this line intersects the top of the paper, draw lines to each endpoint of the dotted line.  These two lines plus the dotted line form a triangle which is the double-layered portion of the folded paper.  WLOG, assume the width of the paper is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />.  The triangle we want to find has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b5172fe9283115da437e2f4957c869b079bac57b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a735c286cc07f695f696da46113d28338d994116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)^{2}+1}=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"177\" height=\"66\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a735c286cc07f695f696da46113d28338d994116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)^{2}+1}=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"177\" height=\"66\" />.  It is an equilateral triangle with height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623fe474cfa16c0ea1a4bbf4ffeb0d4629e2069b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot\\sqrt{3}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"98\" height=\"41\" />, and area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b46b30e39f9b219ebff2e125ddb575e1e61a6b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\cdot1}{2}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"114\" height=\"60\" />.  The area of the paper is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca48e80686018f268d7ce4d5839a4875b8ac2cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot\\sqrt{3}=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, and the folded paper has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f21fc7dca721efb06a7db133053fa18aa2a883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"134\" height=\"41\" />.  The ratio of the area of the folded paper to that of the original paper is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/901d10a205c75d3cc5f3a1d4ada3db7ddd7c6cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\: 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"77\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9ab936eef4c53259854df0f902ee80c3dd8a4d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]import graph; unitsize(3cm); real L = 0.05; pair A = (0,0); pair B = (sqrt(3),0); pair C = (sqrt(3),1); pair D = (0,1); pair X1 = (sqrt(3)/3,0); pair X2= (2*sqrt(3)/3,0); pair Y1 = (2*sqrt(3)/3,1); pair Y2 = (sqrt(3)/3,1); dot(X1); dot(Y1); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(2)); draw(B--D,dashed); draw(X1--Y1,dashed); draw(Y2--X1--D, dotted); draw(X2--Y1--B, dotted);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"148\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2:_FASTEST_SOLUTION.21.21.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2:_FASTEST_SOLUTION!!!\">Solution 2: FASTEST SOLUTION!!!</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2: FASTEST SOLUTION!!!\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Our original paper can be divided like this: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c49f52879d3ae4c96a02111a4524bf2ce73119a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; unitsize(3cm); real L = 0.05; pair A = (0,0); pair B = (sqrt(3),0); pair C = (sqrt(3),1); pair D = (0,1); pair X1 = (sqrt(3)/3,0); pair X2= (2*sqrt(3)/3,0); pair Y1 = (2*sqrt(3)/3,1); pair Y2 = (sqrt(3)/3,1); dot(X1); dot(Y1); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(2)); draw(X1--Y1,dashed); draw(Y2--X1--D, dotted); draw(X2--Y1--B, dotted);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"148\" />\nAfter the fold across the dashed line, our paper becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d37847271f1038d0d9ff92b64959fa4196aaa81f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import graph; unitsize(3cm); real L = 0.05; pair A = (0,0); pair D = (0,1); pair X1 = (sqrt(3)/3,0); pair X2 = (sqrt(3)/6,0.5); pair Y1 = (2*sqrt(3)/3,1); pair Y2 = (sqrt(3)/3,1); pair Z1 = (sqrt(3)/2,1.5); dot(X1); dot(Y1); draw(X1--A--D--Z1--Y1, linewidth(2)); draw(X1--D--Y1); draw(X1--Y1, dashed); draw(Y2--X1,dotted); draw(X2--((sqrt(3)/6 + L/sqrt(3)),(0.5+L/2))); draw(Y2--(sqrt(3)/3,1-L));[/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"218\" />\nSince our original sheet of paper has six congruent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles and and our new one has four, the ratio of the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a436fcb26839c1ec781b56be90f3364bbb8bcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B:A$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/0845add929d0cfe5c876146237d89c70e5fc9a90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4:6\\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} \\: 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"160\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~CHECKMATE2021\n</p><p><br />\n==Solution 3 (Easiest, Intuition)\nThe bottom-right corner will fold onto the top-left corner, then the area of the new figure will have 2 half-triangles on the side along with a big triangle in the middle. The big triangle is simply 2 half-triangles. 2 + 2 = 4, so 4/6 = 2/3, and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Construction\">Construction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Construction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>you could also use your compass to draw a 30 degree angle, make the rectangle, rip it out, and fold it.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ql_90z1m8Qs?si=D8nF9MULxipqoxmc\">https://youtu.be/ql_90z1m8Qs?si=D8nF9MULxipqoxmc</a> ~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2014amc10a/377\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2014amc10a/377</a>\n</p><p>~ ripkobe_745\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jYRA3thX4pI\">https://youtu.be/jYRA3thX4pI</a>\n</p><p>~suprboygamer_jimpop(direct youtube link)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A\">2014 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224418\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 218/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5729/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.242      1 -total\n 62.78%   10.824      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 36.49%    6.291      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12335:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017224418 and revision id 287514. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}